    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d148">

                <pb facs="0198" n="1032" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1032"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/9305</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stovall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-05T14:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 5, 1918, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 7, 11 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3874. Department’s 2117, June 18, 6 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d148-f1"/> Am
                    informed that German black list no longer exists, officially having been
                    withdrawn by German Government about two years ago. There is, however known to
                    be a list of firms located in Switzerland to which permits to forward
                    merchandise through Germany to northern neutrals are steadily refused by German
                    Legation in Berne, but this list is strictly confidential and it is doubtful if
                    it could be obtained.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stovall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d148-f1" n="1" xml:id="d148-f1-content">
                <p>“Can you obtain copy German black list?”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
